{"id":"mahabharata-5-137","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":137,"title":"सप्तत्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 137 · Drona's final warning","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana, downcast and glaring, says nothing, and Bhishma and Drona warn that his pride will bring him to ruin, as a man who wraps himself in a garment thinks it armour. Drona begs him to stop the war for the sake of the Kuru race.","kn":"ಖಿನ್ನನಾಗಿ ಓರೆನೋಟ ಬೀರುವ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಏನೂ ಹೇಳುವುದಿಲ್ಲ; ವಸ್ತ್ರ ಹೊದ್ದವನು ಅದನ್ನೇ ಕವಚವೆಂದು ಭಾವಿಸುವಂತೆ ನಿನ್ನ ಗರ್ವ ವಿನಾಶಕ್ಕೊಯ್ಯುವುದು ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ದ್ರೋಣರು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಕುರುವಂಶಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಯುದ್ಧ ನಿಲ್ಲಿಸೆಂದು ದ್ರೋಣರು ಬೇಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"उदास और तिरछी दृष्टि से देखता दुर्योधन कुछ नहीं कहता, और भीष्म तथा द्रोण चेताते हैं कि उसका अहंकार उसे विनाश तक ले जाएगा, जैसे वस्त्र ओढ़ने वाला उसे कवच समझ ले। द्रोण कुरुवंश के लिए युद्ध रोकने की विनती करते हैं।","te":"విషణ్ణుడై ఓరచూపులు చూస్తున్న దుర్యోధనుడు ఏమీ మాట్లాడడు; వస్త్రం కప్పుకున్నవాడు దానినే కవచమనుకున్నట్లు నీ గర్వం వినాశానికి దారితీస్తుందని భీష్మ ద్రోణులు హెచ్చరిస్తారు. కురువంశం కోసం యుద్ధాన్ని ఆపమని ద్రోణుడు వేడుకుంటాడు.","ta":"மனம் சோர்ந்து ஓரக்கண்ணால் பார்க்கும் துரியோதனன் எதுவும் சொல்லவில்லை; ஆடையைப் போர்த்தியவன் அதைக் கவசம் என்று நினைப்பது போல் உன் செருக்கு அழிவுக்கு இட்டுச் செல்லும் என்று பீஷ்மரும் த்ரோணரும் எச்சரிக்கிறார்கள். குரு குலத்துக்காகப் போரை நிறுத்துமாறு த்ரோணர் வேண்டுகிறார்.","ml":"വിഷാദത്തിലും കണ്ണുരുട്ടിയും ദുര്യോധനൻ ഒന്നും പറയുന്നില്ല; അഹങ്കാരം അവനെ നാശത്തിലെത്തിക്കുമെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മരും ദ്രോണരും മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു; വസ്ത്രം പുതയ്ക്കുന്നവൻ അത് കവചമെന്ന് കരുതുന്നതുപോലെയാണ് അവന്റെ നില. കുരുവംശത്തിനുവേണ്ടി യുദ്ധം നിർത്താൻ ദ്രോണർ അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.137; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु विमनास्तिर्यग्दृष्टिरधोमुखः ।\nसंहत्य च भ्रुवोर्मध्यं न किंचिद्व्याजहार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to in this way, Duryodhana was displeased; looking askance with his face turned down and brows knitted, he said nothing."}},{"n":2,"text":"तं वै विमनसं दृष्ट्वा संप्रेक्ष्यान्योन्यमन्तिकात् ।\nपुनरेवोत्तरं वाक्यमुक्तवन्तौ नरर्षभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him so displeased, the two bulls among men looked at each other close by and spoke to him again."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"शुश्रूषुमनसूयं च ब्रह्मण्यं सत्यसंगरम् ।\nप्रतियोत्स्यामहे पार्थमतो दुःखतरं नु किम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is obedient, free of envy, devoted to brahmins and true to his word. We shall have to fight that Partha; what could be more painful than this?"}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"अश्वत्थाम्नि यथा पुत्रे भूयो मम धनंजये ।\nबहुमानः परो राजन्संनतिश्च कपिध्वजे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As for my son Ashvatthama, so for Dhananjaya, King, I have still greater regard and affection, for the one with the monkey banner."}},{"n":5,"text":"तं चेत्पुत्रात्प्रियतरं प्रतियोत्स्ये धनंजयम् ।\nक्षत्रधर्ममनुष्ठाय धिगस्तु क्षत्रजीविकाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I must fight Dhananjaya, dearer to me than a son, following the duty of a kshatriya, then curse a kshatriya's livelihood."}},{"n":6,"text":"यस्य लोके समो नास्ति कश्चिदन्यो धनुर्धरः ।\nमत्प्रसादात्स बीभत्सुः श्रेयानन्यैर्धनुर्धरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That Bibhatsu, to whom there is no equal among archers in the world, is better than other archers through my favor."}},{"n":7,"text":"मित्रध्रुग्दुष्टभावश्च नास्तिकोऽथानृजुः शठः ।\nन सत्सु लभते पूजां यज्ञे मूर्ख इवागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who betrays friends, whose heart is wicked, who denies the other world, crooked and deceitful, gets no honor among the good, like a fool who has come to a sacrifice."}},{"n":8,"text":"वार्यमाणोऽपि पापेभ्यः पापात्मा पापमिच्छति ।\nचोद्यमानोऽपि पापेन शुभात्मा शुभमिच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even when held back from sins, the sinful-minded wants sin; even when urged on by sin, the good-minded wants good."}},{"n":9,"text":"मिथ्योपचरिता ह्येते वर्तमाना ह्यनु प्रिये ।\nअहितत्वाय कल्पन्ते दोषा भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"These faults, wrongly cared for and followed when they are pleasing, turn out harmful, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":10,"text":"त्वमुक्तः कुरुवृद्धेन मया च विदुरेण च ।\nवासुदेवेन च तथा श्रेयो नैवाभिपद्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have been advised by me, by the Kuru elder, by Vidura, and by Vasudeva too, yet you do not find your good."}},{"n":11,"text":"अस्ति मे बलमित्येव सहसा त्वं तितीर्षसि ।\nसग्राहनक्रमकरं गङ्गावेगमिवोष्णगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking \"I have strength,\" you hastily want to cross, as in summer one would cross the Ganga's current with its crocodiles and sea monsters."}},{"n":12,"text":"वास एव यथा हि त्वं प्रावृण्वानोऽद्य मन्यसे ।\nस्रजं त्यक्तामिव प्राप्य लोभाद्यौधिष्ठिरीं श्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You now think the fortune of Yudhishthira, which you covet in greed, is like a cloth you wear, or a garland someone has cast off."}},{"n":13,"text":"द्रौपदीसहितं पार्थं सायुधैर्भ्रातृभिर्वृतम् ।\nवनस्थमपि राज्यस्थः पाण्डवं कोऽतिजीवति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Partha, with Draupadi, surrounded by his armed brothers, lives in the forest, who living in a kingdom can survive him?"}},{"n":14,"text":"निदेशे यस्य राजानः सर्वे तिष्ठन्ति किंकराः ।\nतमैलविलमासाद्य धर्मराजो व्यराजत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharmaraja, whose command all the kings stood waiting on as servants, shone when he reached Ailavila."}},{"n":15,"text":"कुबेरसदनं प्राप्य ततो रत्नान्यवाप्य च ।\nस्फीतमाक्रम्य ते राष्ट्रं राज्यमिच्छन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having reached Kubera's abode and gained jewels there, the Pandavas, having attacked your prosperous realm, now want the kingdom."}},{"n":16,"text":"दत्तं हुतमधीतं च ब्राह्मणास्तर्पिता धनैः ।\nआवयोर्गतमायुश्च कृतकृत्यौ च विद्धि नौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have given, offered sacrifice, studied, and satisfied brahmins with wealth, and our lives are spent. Know that we two have done what we had to do."}},{"n":17,"text":"त्वं तु हित्वा सुखं राज्यं मित्राणि च धनानि च ।\nविग्रहं पाण्डवैः कृत्वा महद्व्यसनमाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But you, giving up pleasure, kingdom, friends and wealth, and making war with the Pandavas, will fall into great calamity."}},{"n":18,"text":"द्रौपदी यस्य चाशास्ते विजयं सत्यवादिनी ।\nतपोघोरव्रता देवी न त्वं जेष्यसि पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whose victory the truthful Draupadi wishes, the goddess of terrible vows and austerity: you will not conquer that Pandava."}},{"n":19,"text":"मन्त्री जनार्दनो यस्य भ्राता यस्य धनंजयः ।\nसर्वशस्त्रभृतां श्रेष्ठं कथं जेष्यसि पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His counselor is Janardana and his brother is Dhananjaya; how will you conquer that Pandava, best of all bearers of weapons?"}},{"n":20,"text":"सहाया ब्राह्मणा यस्य धृतिमन्तो जितेन्द्रियाः ।\nतमुग्रतपसं वीरं कथं जेष्यसि पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How will you conquer that hero of fierce austerity, whose helpers are steadfast brahmins who have mastered their senses?"}},{"n":21,"text":"पुनरुक्तं च वक्ष्यामि यत्कार्यं भूतिमिच्छता ।\nसुहृदा मज्जमानेषु सुहृत्सु व्यसनार्णवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will say again what a friend who wants your welfare must say, when friends are sinking in a sea of calamity:"}},{"n":22,"text":"अलं युद्धेन तैर्वीरैः शाम्य त्वं कुरुवृद्धये ।\nमा गमः ससुतामात्यः सबलश्च पराभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"enough of war with those heroes. Make peace for the growth of the Kurus. Do not go to defeat with your sons, ministers and army.\""}}]}]}